I discarded the 3 of clubs and one 7, so the pair is broken. Your lowest two cards were the 3 and a seven. I kept the other 7, the K, the 9 and the new cards. You drew the 6 of clubs and the jack of diamonds. You now hold K, 9, 7, 6, J with no pair. I stood pat, so the dealer still has five cards. The final betting round is yours.

